    "checks": [
      "An accessory apartment is permitted by right in R-3 and by special exception (Zoning Hearing Board) in A, R-1, R-2, C-1 and INS (Tables IV-1 #33, V-1 #46, VI-1 #69). It is not permitted in C-2, VIL or PO",
      "One per single-family detached lot. It may be inside the house, attached, or detached (245-14.3B). The definition speaks of a unit 'in or added to an existing single-family detached dwelling' (245-2.1)",
      "Size: at least 300 sq ft and no more than 45% of the primary structure's total floor area (245-14.3G)",
      "The owner must live in one of the units, except for bona fide temporary absences (245-14.3E)",
      "A complete separate housekeeping unit with its own outside entrance, not on the front facade of the house (245-14.3A)",
      "It must meet the district setbacks and coverage. A detached apartment must be at least 10 ft from the house (245-14.3D)",
      "At least three off-street parking spaces in total for the owner and the tenant (245-14.3H)",
      "It may not be subdivided or sold apart from the house (245-14.3I)",
      "Accessory buildings: not in the front yard, 5 ft from lot lines, 20 ft high at most (245-16.2). Whether 20 ft binds a detached apartment is not stated in 245-14.3",
      "R-2 and R-3 tables give lot size 'per dwelling unit'. Whether the apartment needs its own share is not settled",
      "The definition ('in or added to an existing single-family detached dwelling', 245-2.1) and 245-14.3B ('may be detached or attached', 2025) conflict on whether a detached apartment or one with a new house is allowed. Ask the Township",
      "Minimum habitable floor area: 'accessory dwelling units' at least 400 sq ft, or 350 sq ft for one occupant (245-16.7). 245-14.3G says 300 sq ft. The larger figure is shown",
      "Conversion apartments (special exception in R-3): no outside alterations except for fire protection, no more than two units added, one common principal entrance kept (245-14.20)"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Upper Allen Township (uatwp.org). Read on eCode360 (UP1380) in a browser, one print view at a time. Code searches on 2026-11-14 for accessory dwelling, accessory apartment, in-law, ECHO, elder cottage, family care and accessory residential found the use only in 245-2.1, 245-14.3 and the use tables 245-4.2, 245-5.2 and 245-6.2. Industrial district tables do not list it. Zoning Hearing Board agendas (2022 to 2026) show special exception requests for accessory apartments, including a detached one on 2026-08-13."
  },
